<https://metabolinkai.net/quotient/exampleStatement/6a3c5a7b956260ca304ac178b88de37d1550fc99e1ad4b695ff6237dc11ff4d9>
        <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object>
                "The aim of the present AOP is to construct a linear pathway that captures the KEs and KERs that occur after binding of antagonist to NMDA receptor in neurons during development in hippocampus and cortex. All KEs of the AOP are characterised by STRONG essentiality for the AO (learning and memory impairment). Similarly, the biological plausibility in the majority of KERs is rated STRONG as there is extensive mechanistic understanding. However, the empirical support for the present KERs cannot be rated high as in most occasions the KEup and KEdowm of a KER have not been investigated simultaneously under the same experimental protocol.\n";
        <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate>
                <http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C25217>;
